  "language_probability": 1,
  "text": "This vacuum cleaner lifts dirt from the floor and carries it into a collection bin. It does this by creating a continuous airflow, not by pulling on each particle directly. An electric motor spins a fan that pushes air out of the cleaner. That lowers the air pressure inside, so room air rushes in through the nozzle. The moving air carries loose dust and debris along the suction path. A cyclone or filter separates the dirt from that air before the air leaves the machine. A clogged filter restricts air flow, which is why cleaning it can restore cleaning performance. So the fan starts an air flow and the moving air transports dirt into the vacuum.",
